ITEMS = ((('what should i do for an unconscious person', 'how do i help someone who is unconscious', 'what is the first aid for an unconscious person', 'how to respond when a person is unconscious', 'what to do when someone will not wake up for an unconscious person', 'how do you care for an unconscious casualty', 'what helps an unconscious person when someone is unconscious', 'how can i assist an unconscious person safely', 'what is the best response to unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'how should i handle an unresponsive person'), 'Check if the person responds and shout for help. Call emergency services, open the airway and check breathing, then place them in the recovery position if breathing or start CPR if not. Stay with them until a qualified person arrives.'), (('how do i check if someone is unconscious', 'how long to shake and shout at an unconscious person', 'what if the person is hard to wake', 'how to check response in an unconscious person', 'can an unconscious person hear me', 'how to tell confusion from unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'what to do if someone is very drowsy for an unconscious person', 'how to check breathing in an unconscious person', 'what if the person responds slowly', 'when to treat someone as unconscious'), 'Try gentle shaking and a loud shout to see if the person responds. If they do not, or only moan, treat them as unconscious and call emergency services. Check breathing and send someone to fetch help while you stay with them.'), (('should i shake an unconscious person', 'is it safe to move an unconscious person', 'how to handle an unconscious body', 'what if moving an unconscious person causes pain', 'should i slap an unconscious person', 'how to avoid harming an unconscious casualty', 'what if the person fell from height', 'how to support the head of an unconscious person', 'when not to move someone who is unconscious', 'who can advise about moving a casualty for an unconscious person'), 'Shake gently by the shoulders and shout rather than slapping or jolting the person. Avoid moving them if a neck or spinal injury is possible unless you must protect the airway. Call emergency services and follow their guidance about moving.'), (('what if an unconscious person is not breathing', 'should i start cpr for an unconscious person', 'how to check breathing in an unresponsive adult for an unconscious person', 'what does agonal breathing mean for an unconscious person', 'how long to look for breathing for an unconscious person', 'what to do if there is no chest movement for an unconscious person', 'should i give rescue breaths first for an unconscious person', 'how to begin compressions on an unconscious person', 'what if the person is gasping', 'when to call emergency services for no breathing for an unconscious person'), 'If an unconscious person is not breathing normally, call emergency services and start CPR with firm chest compressions. Gasping is not normal breathing. Continue until a qualified team takes over, and send someone to find a defibrillator if possible.'), (('what if an unconscious person is breathing normally', 'should i use the recovery position for an unconscious person', 'how to place an unconscious person on their side', 'what to do while waiting with a breathing casualty for an unconscious person', "how to monitor an unconscious person's breathing", 'what if the person vomits while unconscious', 'should i cover an unconscious person', 'can i give water to an unconscious person', 'how to keep the airway clear for an unconscious person', 'when to roll an unconscious person'), 'If an unconscious person is breathing normally, roll them into the recovery position to keep the airway clear. Check breathing regularly and keep them warm with a coat or blanket. Never give food or drink, and call emergency services.'), (('how do i open the airway of an unconscious person', 'should i tilt the head back for an unconscious person', 'what is the jaw thrust technique for an unconscious person', 'how to check for an object in the mouth for an unconscious person', 'should i sweep a finger in the mouth for an unconscious person', 'what if the tongue falls back for an unconscious person', 'how to lift the chin safely for an unconscious person', 'what if the neck may be injured for an unconscious person', 'how to keep the airway clear while waiting for an unconscious person', 'who should check an unconscious airway'), 'Tilt the head back and lift the chin to open the airway, unless a neck injury is suspected. Look in the mouth and remove only a clearly visible object. Do not blind sweep, and call emergency services if breathing is difficult.'), (('what causes a person to become unconscious', 'can fainting cause unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'what medical problems lead to unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'can a head injury cause someone to pass out for an unconscious person', 'what if an unconscious person has diabetes', 'can low blood sugar cause unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'what if an unconscious person has had a seizure', 'how to tell the cause of unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'why did a person collapse suddenly', 'who can diagnose the cause for an unconscious person'), 'Unconsciousness can follow fainting, head injury, seizures, low blood sugar or serious illness. You do not need to know the cause to give first aid: check breathing, call emergency services and treat what you find. Tell the crew any relevant history you know.'), (('should i give sugar to an unconscious person', 'can i give medicine to someone who is unconscious', 'what if an unconscious person is diabetic', 'should i put anything in the mouth for an unconscious person', 'can i give water to an unconscious casualty', 'what if the person has tablets with them', 'is it safe to give glucose gel for an unconscious person', 'how to help a person with low blood sugar', 'when to ask a qualified person about medication', 'what not to give an unconscious person'), 'Never give food, drink or tablets to an unconscious person because they may choke. If you know they have diabetes, tell emergency services when you call. A trained person may give glucose gel once the airway is safe, but do not attempt it yourself.'), (('what if an unconscious person starts fitting', 'how to protect someone who is fitting and unconscious', 'can a seizure cause unconsciousness for an unconscious person', 'should i hold a fitting person down', 'how to time a seizure in an unconscious person', 'what to do after a fit ends for an unconscious person', 'should i put something in the mouth during a fit for an unconscious person', 'how to place a person after a seizure', 'when to call emergency services for a fit for an unconscious person', 'who can assess after a seizure for an unconscious person'), 'If a person fits, protect them from injury, do not hold them down and do not put anything in the mouth. Once the fit stops, check breathing and place them in the recovery position. Call emergency services, especially if the fit is prolonged or repeated.'), (('when should i call emergency services for an unconscious person', 'is unconsciousness always an emergency for an unconscious person', 'how quickly must i call for help for an unconscious person', 'what if the person wakes up quickly', 'should i call for a brief faint for an unconscious person', 'what to tell the operator about an unconscious person', 'how long to wait before calling for an unconscious person', 'what if breathing is normal but the person will not wake', 'should i stay with an unconscious person', 'when to hand over to a qualified person'), 'Call emergency services for any person who is unconscious or hard to wake, even if they recover quickly. Tell the operator where you are and what you observed. Stay with the person, keep the airway open and hand over when help arrives.'))
